Attaching a meta
description: the .yo/meta.yo overlay and the !!<...> tag - two routes to one vocabulary
- >
  **Two ways to attach.** A directory's `.yo/meta.yo` overlay nests under the JSON-Schema keywords, so
  the engine maps a meta-path to an instance-path (`properties: age` annotates the instance node
  `age`). In a file, the `!!<...>` tag attaches a meta to the value that follows it - or, alone at the
  top, to the document root. The tag's contents are themselves yamlover: a pointer to a hosted schema,
  or an inline schema literal - a one-off format needs no named definition. json5p has no tags:
  overlay only.
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  !!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>     # a pointer to a hosted schema
  My Article
  - !!<format: text/x-plantuml> |   # an inline schema literal - itself
    @startuml                       #   a one-line yamlover/meta document
    ...
